\section{Use case}{

This store is the streaming expression backend for datasets too large to
hold in memory as a sparse matrix. It is slotted into \code{exprObj@exprMat}
like any other disk-backed store; downstream Giotto methods that recognize
the class dispatch to streaming implementations, which read the triplet
payload in cell chunks rather than materializing the whole matrix.
}

\section{Subset semantics}{

\code{parquetExprStore} supports lightweight subsetting via the \code{[} operator.
\code{pe[i, j]} returns a new store whose \code{feat_ids} / \code{cell_ids} are narrowed
to the kept rows / columns and whose \code{gene_idx} / \code{cell_idx} slots record
the \emph{original} parquet positions of the kept entries. The Parquet file
on disk is \strong{not} rewritten -- \code{storeRead()} filters lazily via Arrow
using the recorded indices, so chained subsets stay cheap.
}

